# PocketOS: telnetd stays available for local use only. The vendor image
# exposes a passwordless root login on telnet to the whole LAN; binding to
# loopback closes that without removing the service (Buildroot's S50telnet
# reads TELNETD_ARGS from this file). Serial console and SSH (after `passwd`
# on the console) are the remote paths.
TELNETD_ARGS="-F -b 127.0.0.1"
